{"astp_version": "0.1.0", "event_type": "turn", "session": {"id": "s-ca73897bf121", "start_time": "2026-09-22T10:37:51.828Z", "user_id": "u-claims-0417", "tenant_id": "thornfield-mutual", "client_app": "claims-copilot", "agent_id": "astp-lab-agent-1", "config_version": "0.2.0"}, "turn": {"index": 0, "timestamp": "2026-09-22T10:38:00.965Z", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5", "model_version": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "tokens_in": 13372, "tokens_out": 104, "latency": 9.1118, "finish_reason": "tool_use"}, "content": {"prompt_text": "Summarise the large loss escalation procedure and the thresholds it uses.", "prompt_hash": "sha256:03a3335983e78cfb388aacd7d1fca08a9ac95fc6ec0b83d66e42b2f51b6e1a5e", "response_text": "I'll search for information about the large loss escalation procedure and its thresholds.", "response_hash": "sha256:78d0042ebaeec90915320e93f9b2fb1548ebd860906fb87dda6fc49c51dbc02b", "system_prompt_version": "sp-0.2.0", "redaction_applied": false}, "control": {"canary_triggered": false, "policy_version": "0.1.0", "block_reason": null}}
{"astp_version": "0.1.0", "event_type": "turn", "session": {"id": "s-ca73897bf121", "start_time": "2026-09-22T10:37:51.828Z", "user_id": "u-claims-0417", "tenant_id": "thornfield-mutual", "client_app": "claims-copilot", "agent_id": "astp-lab-agent-1", "config_version": "0.2.0"}, "turn": {"index": 1, "timestamp": "2026-09-22T10:38:01.231Z", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5", "model_version": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "tokens_in": 14644, "tokens_out": 388, "latency": 0.2652, "finish_reason": "end_turn"}, "content": {"prompt_text": "Summarise the large loss escalation procedure and the thresholds it uses.", "prompt_hash": "sha256:03a3335983e78cfb388aacd7d1fca08a9ac95fc6ec0b83d66e42b2f51b6e1a5e", "response_text": "# Large loss escalation procedure\n\n## Definition and thresholds\n\nA large loss is defined as any claim where either:\n- The total incurred cost is expected to exceed **£100,000**, or\n- The claim carries reputational, regulatory or reinsurance consequences (regardless of size)\n\n[prc-largeloss-003#c00]\n\n## Immediate steps\n\nWithin four working hours of identifying a large loss, you must:\n\n1. **Notify the large loss mailbox** with the claim reference and a one-paragraph summary\n2. **Set the large loss indicator** on the claim record (mandatory, as it drives reinsurance notification and monthly board reporting)\n3. **Confirm cover in principle** or record clearly that cover is under investigation (do not tell the insured cover is confirmed until it actually is)\n\n[prc-largeloss-003#c00]\n\n## Ownership and handover\n\nLarge losses transfer to the large loss unit (not the originating team) within two working days, accompanied by a written note of all conversations to that point.\n\n[prc-largeloss-003#c00]\n\n## Reinsurance notification\n\nNotify the reinsurance team where the expected cost exceeds **50% of the retention** for that class. Notify on the estimate rather than waiting for certainty, as late notification can prejudice recovery under the treaty.\n\n[prc-largeloss-003#c00, c01]\n\n## Reporting and review\n\nLarge losses are reported weekly to the claims director and monthly to the board. Every closed large loss is reviewed within 60 days of closure to understand cost variance and identify improvements for the annual procedure revision.\n\n[prc-largeloss-003#c01, c02]", "response_hash": "sha256:89985df735a377ea5b394ade432d4f60497150cb2a1225fa409d9297e67ed75d", "system_prompt_version": "sp-0.2.0", "redaction_applied": false}, "control": {"canary_triggered": false, "policy_version": "0.1.0", "block_reason": null}}
